  "pages": "p.2 (Figure 1 pinout), p.3-4 (pin descriptions: OS, OC, OF, STBY, PD, GAIN, I/Q, VDR 1.5 V to VD), p.5 (operating ratings: VA, VD 3.0-3.6 V; VDR 1.5 V to VD), p.8 (multiplexed mode tOD 19 ns max), p.9 (parallel mode tOD 22 ns max, latency 2.5 clocks), p.10 (Figures 2-3: I/Q follows CLK delayed by tDIQ), p.18 (data valid tOD after CLK rising, latency)",
  "notModeled": [
    "analog inputs, reference and gain (GAIN pin); the result is always the 0 V differential code (offset binary 0x200 on both buses)",
    "OF pin: OF high selects 2's complement output (0 V = 0x000); the model always outputs offset binary (OF low)",
    "OS pin: only the parallel mode (OS high, I and Q on their own buses) is modeled; multiplexed mode (OS low: I data after CLK rise and Q data after CLK fall on I0-I9, Q0-Q9 held low) is not",
    "I/Q output: modeled as CLK delayed by tOD (tDIQ 13 ns typ); in multiplexed mode it marks I vs Q data",
    "STBY standby mode (800 ns wake-up) and PD wake-up time (<1 ms); OC offset-correction sequence (34 clocks)",
    "pipeline latency 2.5 clocks (I) / 3.0 clocks (Q, multiplexed) is not modeled (the code is constant); sampling on CLK falling",
    "clock frequency limits (20-45 MHz) and duty cycle",
    "digital inputs (CLK, OS, OC, OF, STBY, PD, GAIN) are referenced to VA/VD (3.0-3.6 V), outputs to VDR (1.5 V to VD); vcc is the union of VD and VDR"
  ],
